# Battle Arena Realtime — Architecture

- This service is a **transport / presence boundary only**. Laravel owns authentication, authorization, game rules, battle results, XP rewards, and PostgreSQL persistence.
- An authenticated WebSocket is **not** authorization to join any battle room. Phase 5A ships connection bootstrap only — no PvP, matchmaking, invites, or battle rooms.
- Keep this repository independent. Do not merge into `battle-arena-api`, `battle-arena-web`, `battle-arena-mobile`, or `battle-arena-infra`. Infra Compose orchestrates; it does not own Node source.
- Never port the PvE Battle Engine, damage formulas, trainer XP rules, or creature entitlements into Node.
- Never trust client-supplied `player_id`, `battle_id`, `trainer_level`, or `is_admin`. Identity comes only from atomically redeemed Laravel tickets.
- Do not install Socket.IO or Laravel Reverb. Use native `ws` (RFC 6455) only.
- Read `battle-arena-api/docs/PHASE5A_REALTIME_NODE_WEBSOCKET_SPEC_EN.md` before changing architecture or protocol.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — game authority in the gateway
socket.on("message", (raw) => applyDamage(JSON.parse(raw)));

// ✅ GOOD — transport session only
// After ticket redemption, emit connection.ready; reject gameplay frames in 5A.
```
